- @title = 'What\'s new · Nitrous'
- @html_class = 'light'
- @body_id = 'whatsnew'
- @body_class = 'introducing'

.page
  .page-hero
    .container
      = render partial: 'layouts/webnav', locals: { active: 'whatsnew' }

      .hero-visual
        = image_tag 'home/nitrous-pro-chrome.png', width: '970px', alt: 'Nitrous Pro'

      .hero-tagline
        h2 Introducing Nitrous Pro
        h3 Software Development Without the Pain
        = render 'layouts/cta_form'


  article.centered
    .container

      .grid-wrapper

        .grid-item
          = image_tag 'home/whatsnew-1.jpg', alt: 'Nitrous Pro'
          h3.new
            em New
            | Revamped IDE
          p Reworked from the ground up, the new Nitrous IDE is cleaner, and faster than ever

        .grid-item
          = image_tag 'home/whatsnew-2.jpg', alt: 'Nitrous Pro'
          h3.new
            em New
            | Improved collaboration
          p Code collaboration has been greatly improved, and is now faster and more robust

        .grid-item
          = image_tag 'home/whatsnew-3.jpg', alt: 'Nitrous Pro'
          h3.new
            em New
            | More Stacks
          p New and updated templates have been added (including Java, Wordpress, Laravel)

        .grid-item
          = image_tag 'home/whatsnew-4.jpg', alt: 'Nitrous Pro'
          h3.new
            em New
            | Improved editor themes
          p Nitrous Pro introduces new light and dark themes, with improved syntax highlighting

        .grid-item
          = image_tag 'home/whatsnew-5.jpg', alt: 'Nitrous Pro'
          h3.new
            em New
            | Split editing
          p You can now have multiple files opened at once thanks to the new split editing mode

        .grid-item
          = image_tag 'home/whatsnew-6.jpg', alt: 'Nitrous Pro'
          h3.new
            | Manage your dedicated box
          p Comes with Nitrous's powerful and easy-to-use workspace &amp; container management dashboard


  article.two-blocks
    .left
      .table
        .col
          .row.title
            span Pro
          .row
            span
              i.fa.fa-check
              | Whole new IDE
          .row
            span
              i.fa.fa-check
              | Full root access
          .row
            span
              i.fa.fa-check
              | Auto-save
          .row
            span
              i.fa.fa-check
              | Private, dedicated machine
          .row
            span
              i.fa.fa-check
              | Fully configurable containers

          a.btn.blue-outline href="/features" Learn more about Pro

    .right
      .table
        .col
          .row.title
            span Lite
          .row
            span
              i.fa.fa-minus
              | Previous IDE version
          .row
            span
              i.fa.fa-minus
              | No root access
          .row
            span
              i.fa.fa-minus
              | Manual file save
          .row
            span
              i.fa.fa-minus
              | Shared resources
          .row
            span
              i.fa.fa-minus
              | Very limited configuration

          a.btn.grey-outline href="https://lite.nitrous.io" Go to lite.nitrous.io
  

  article.parallax
    .container
      = image_tag 'home/nitrous-pro-chrome-2.png', width: '1024px', alt: 'Nitrous Pro', class: 'parallaxEl'


  article.qa
    .container
      h3.big-title Questions and Answers
      .columns
        .item
          h4 What are the biggest differences between Nitrous Pro and the original Nitrous (Nitrous Lite)?
          p Nitrous Pro is a completely new and separate platform that requires a new account login. The biggest difference is that Nitrous Pro runs on your own, dedicated cloud machine. This enables us to provide root access to all users, and also improves stability and performance across the board.
        
        .item
          h4 How long will I be able to access my old Nitrous account?
          p 
            ' Your old Nitrous account will be accessible at https://lite.nitrous.io until we sunset the old product on July 1st, 2015. If you have files that you would like to move to Nitrous Pro, you can read about migration options 
            a href="http://docs.nitrous.io/v1.0/docs/migrate-your-data-to-the-new-platform" here
            ' . If you were using the original Nitrous (Nitrous Lite) for a workshop or class, please
            a href="mailto:pro@nitrous.io" contact us 
            |  and we will discuss migration options for your class and students.
        
        .item
          h4 Can I still sign up for a paid plan on the original Nitrous?
          p As of Wednesday April 22nd, you can only purchase paid plans on Nitrous Pro.
        
        .item
          h4 Will my account be converted to Pro automatically?
          p 
            | Your account 
            strong will not 
            | be converted automatically. Nitrous Pro and Nitrous Lite (the original Nitrous) are completely separate products. You will need to 
            a href="https://pro.nitrous.io/app/#/signup" create a new account 
            | for Nitrous Pro. If you are having trouble creating a new account or you are a paid user on Nitrous Lite, please 
            a href="mailto:pro@nitrous.io" send us an email
            | .
        
        .item
          h4 Do I need to migrate my boxes to Nitrous Pro?
          p 
            | We provide all of the same starter templates on Nitrous Pro that we had on previous versions, so you are not required to migrate boxes. If you have some customizations that you would like to migrate, you can check out this help article with more details 
            a href="http://docs.nitrous.io/v1.0/docs/migrate-your-data-to-the-new-platform" here
            | . If you made specific customizations that you're having difficulty getting up and running on Nitrous Pro, please 
            a href="mailto:pro@nitrous.io" contact us
            | .
        
        .item
          h4 I'm an educator and you just broke my workflow! What do I do now?
          p
            ' We will continue to support educational organizations with Nitrous Pro and do have a free tier available, especially for qualified educational, not-for-profit organizations. Please 
            a href="mailto:pro@nitrous.io" contact us 
            ' so we can set up your organization with the appropriate transition plan.

        .item
          h4 I'm a paid user on the original Nitrous (Nitrous Lite). How do I move to Nitrous Pro?
          p
            ' You will need to create a completely
            a href="https://pro.nitrous.io/app/#/signup" new account 
            ' on Nitrous Pro, and then you will need to cancel your account on the original Nitrous.

        .item
          h4 How will pricing change?
          p
            ' Individual pricing plans on Nitrous are currently 
            a href="https://pro.nitrous.io/pricing" $15, $30, and $65
            '  for Basic, Standard, and Pro plans respectively.

        .item
          h4 In what ways did you improve the IDE?
          p
            ' We've added split pane editing, a more intuitive collaboration workflow, additional themes, better GitHub integration, and have generally streamlined the design to allow for more focus on your code. More details on Nitrous Pro features can be found 
            a href="https://pro.nitrous.io/features/" here
            | .

        .item
          h4 How does the free plan work on Nitrous Pro?
          p
            ' Providing dedicated cloud virtual machines to hundreds of thousands of developers while maintaining superior performance is a difficult technical problem. A minority of users also unfortunately don't follow our 
            a href="http://help.nitrous.io/admin-terms/" terms of service
            ' , which makes providing an unlimited free tier a difficult task.
          p In an effort to maintain the best user experience for all of our users, the free workspace on Nitrous Pro is limited to 2 hours of usage per day, and then will automatically shut down. We also require free users to verify themselves with a mobile phone number, to restrict the amount of abuse on free accounts.
          p We've found the 2 hour limit is sufficient for a reasonable amount of usage and enables most developers to benefit from the system while still allowing us to provide the best experience possible
          p If you are using Nitrous for more than 2 hours per day, we hope you consider a paid subscription with unlimited hours.


      p.centered.solo
        | Have more questions? Please feel free to&nbsp;
        a href="mailto:hello@nitrous.io" target="_blank" send us a message
        | .


  = render partial: 'layouts/cta', locals: { theme: 'darker' }

= render partial: 'layouts/footer', locals: { active: 'whatsnew' }

